@page
@model ExperienceModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Experience";
}

<section class="page-hero page-container">
    <div class="eyebrow">CAREER TIMELINE</div>
    <h1>Experience that compounds.</h1>
    <p>Selected roles, responsibilities, and the kind of problems I've enjoyed solving.</p>
</section>

<section class="timeline page-container">
     
    <article class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-date">2012 — 2023</div>
        <div class="timeline-node"></div>
        <div class="timeline-content glass-card">
            <div class="role-header">
                <div><h2>Senior Software Developer</h2><h3>PNI Digital Media</h3></div>
                <span class="role-type">FULL-TIME</span>
            </div>
            <p>Lead developer for customer-facing web platforms and internal systems serving a growing user base.</p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    Developed C# / Web API microservices supporting order fulfillment, payments, transportation, and external system integrations.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Modernized legacy systems into cloud-based microservices using Azure, AWS, Docker, RabbitMQ, Redis, and Blob Storage.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Developed a media-transfer platform capable of moving hundreds of thousands of assets to Azure Blob Storage.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Implemented centralized logging using Elasticsearch, Logstash, Kibana, and RabbitMQ.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Built and maintained public/private APIs with comprehensive technical documentation, architecture diagrams, and process documentation.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Managed development infrastructure including Windows Server, IIS, SQL Server, Git, TFS, RabbitMQ, and SharePoint.
                </li>
            </ul>
            <div class="tag-row"><span>C#</span><span>ASP.NET Core</span><span>SQL Server</span><span>Azure</span></div>
        </div>
    </article>
      
    <article class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-date">2011 — 2012</div>
        <div class="timeline-node"></div>
        <div class="timeline-content glass-card">
            <div class="role-header">
                <div><h2>Intermediate Software Developer</h2><h3>CAMS Software Corporation</h3></div>
                <span class="role-type">FULL-TIME</span>
            </div>
            <p>Built business applications and integrations for operations, reporting, and customer workflows.</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Delivered reusable APIs and data-access components across multiple products.</li>
                <li>
                    Built a transportation routing engine that optimized truck routes, reducing mileage and operating costs.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Provided ongoing technical support and software updates for clients.
                </li>
            </ul>
            <div class="tag-row"><span>.NET</span><span>REST</span><span>WPF</span><span>Visual Basic</span></div>
        </div>
    </article>
     
    <article class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-date">2011 — 2011</div>
        <div class="timeline-node"></div>
        <div class="timeline-content glass-card">
            <div class="role-header">
                <div><h2>Junior Software Developer</h2><h3>Equinox Software</h3></div>
                <span class="role-type">FULL-TIME</span>
            </div>
            <p>Build customer facing web applications for an airline company.</p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    Developed business applications for power utility and airline clients.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Built an email marketing platform supporting 100,000+ monthly recipients with newsletter generation and tracking.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Gathered requirements, created prototypes, and implemented production applications with designers.
                </li>
            </ul>
            <div class="tag-row"><span>Classic ASP</span><span>VBScript</span><span>SQL</span><span>UI Design</span></div>
        </div>
    </article>
   
    <article class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-date">2010 — 2010</div>
        <div class="timeline-node"></div>
        <div class="timeline-content glass-card">
            <div class="role-header">
                <div><h2>Junior Software Developer</h2><h3>Tigereyesoft</h3></div>
                <span class="role-type">FULL-TIME</span>
            </div>
            <p>Developed .NET application that utilized Microsoft's WPF UI Technology for creating a versitile Windows application. </p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    Developed .NET applications for time-management systems and assisted with Windows Server administration.
                </li> 
            </ul>
            <div class="tag-row"><span>C#</span><span>WPF</span><span>SQL</span><span>Git</span></div>
        </div>
    </article> 

    <article class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-date">2008 — 2009</div>
        <div class="timeline-node"></div>
        <div class="timeline-content glass-card">
            <div class="role-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>
                        Help Desk/Domain Administrator
                    </h2><h3>Mark Anthony Group</h3>
                </div>
                <span class="role-type">FULL-TIME</span>
            </div>
            <p>Worked as a domain administrator, managing a companies users and companies domain resources.</p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    Provided employee technical support and assisted with Windows Server and Active Directory administration.
                </li> 
            </ul>
            <div class="tag-row"><span>Windows Server</span><span>Active Directory</span><span>Databases</span><span>Workflows</span></div>
        </div>
    </article>
</section>
